WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.820
Almost finished, yet public works remain stalled.

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:08.800
At the reporting date, Peru had 2,262 stalled
public works projects.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:14.540
Of those, 281 reported more than 90%
construction progress.

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:20.160
155 of them had no recorded budget
allocation for 2026.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:25.420
Without funding, the remaining work
cannot go ahead.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:30.320
The OECD warns that failing to secure funding
from one year to the next causes delays.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:35.980
When funding runs short, communities may
have to keep waiting for public services.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:41.520
Meanwhile, 23 projects reported 100%
construction progress and were still listed as stalled.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:48.220
A finished structure does not guarantee
the public service is up and running.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:51.920
How can we make sure these projects
deliver what they were built for?

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:56.860
Explore the dashboard, its sources,
and the projects that warrant a closer look.
